<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Rassini places $70 million debt issue.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Rassini places $70 million debt issue.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rassini SA, a subsidiary of SanLuis Corp, said on Tuesday that it has placed $70 million in long-term debt in markets in the United States and Europe.</p>
<p>The debt, which comes due in 2003, is backed by future exports of automobile suspension parts.</p>
<p>The company said that the issue received an investment grade rating of BBB- from rating agency Duff &amp; Phelps.</p>
<p>Rassini said the funds from the issue will be used to pay off short-term debt.</p>
<p>Lead manager was BT Securities, a subsidiary of Bankers Trust Corp.</p>
<p>-- Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559</p>
